00:56:26,666 --> 00:56:32,666
Hidden Figures is a 2016 American biographical drama film co-produced and directed by
Theodore Melfi, who co-wrote the screenplay with Allison Schroeder.

13
01:01:08,888 --> 01:01:14,888
It is loosely based on the 2016 book by Margot Lee Shetterly.

14
01:05:51,111 --> 01:05:57,111
It follows three female African-American
mathematicians, Katherine Goble Johnson (Taraji P.

15
01:10:33,333 --> 01:10:39,333
Henson), Dorothy Vaughan (Octavia Spencer), and Mary Jackson (Janelle Monáe),
who worked at NASA during the Space Race in the 1950s and 1960s.

16
01:15:15,555 --> 01:15:21,555
Other stars include Kevin Costner, Kirsten Dunst, Jim Parsons,
Mahershala Ali, Aldis Hodge, and Glen Powell.

17
01:19:57,777 --> 01:20:03,777
Principal photography began in March 2016 in Atlanta,
Georgia, and wrapped up in May 2016.

18
01:24:40,000 --> 01:24:46,000
Other filming locations included several other locations in Georgia,
including East Point, Canton, Monroe, Columbus, and Madison.

19
01:29:22,222 --> 01:29:28,222
Hidden Figures had a limited release on December 25, 2016, by 20th
Century Fox, before going wide in on January 6, 2017.

20
01:34:04,444 --> 01:34:10,444
The film received positive reviews, with praise for the performances (particularly Henson, Spencer and Monáe), the writing, direction,
cinematography, emotional tone, and historical accuracy, although some argued it featured a white savior narrative.

21
01:38:46,666 --> 01:38:52,666
The film was a commercial success, grossing $236 million
worldwide against its $25 million production budget.

22
01:43:28,888 --> 01:43:34,888
Deadline Hollywood noted it as one of the most profitable releases of 2016,
and estimated that it made a net profit of $95.5 million.

23
01:48:11,111 --> 01:48:17,111
The film was chosen by the National Board of Review as one of the top ten films of 2016 and received various awards
and nominations, including three nominations at the 89th Academy Awards, including Best Picture.

24
01:52:53,333 --> 01:52:59,333
It also won the Screen Actors Guild Award for Outstanding
Performance by a Cast in a Motion Picture.

25
01:57:35,555 --> 01:57:41,555
The film explores themes of nasa, mathematics,
sexism, biography, racial segregation.

26
02:02:17,777 --> 02:02:23,777
The tone is emotional.
